{"trial": "t01", "round": 1, "status": "ok", "dev_success": 0.3262, "train_success_last10pct": 0.3028, "wall_s": 105.7, "params": 54278, "config": {"lr": 0.0005, "lr_schedule": "linear_decay", "n_envs": 256, "rollout_len": 16, "ppo_epochs": 2, "n_minibatches": 4, "gamma": 0.95, "gae_lambda": 0.9, "clip_eps": 0.2, "ent_coef": 0.01, "vf_coef": 0.5, "max_grad_norm": 1.0, "adv_norm": true, "encoder": "conv", "width": 64, "depth": 2, "activation": "relu", "norm": "none", "obs_mode": "voxels", "reward_mode": "cells", "success_bonus": 5.0, "step_penalty": 0.0}, "your_hypothesis": "Raising the success bonus from 1 to 5 makes an exact match worth much more than collecting per-cell reward, which should push the agent to get the order and overhangs right and then stop. If dev success doesn't improve, the reward signal is not what limits learning."}
{"trial": "t02", "round": 1, "status": "ok", "dev_success": 0.5625, "train_success_last10pct": 0.5469, "wall_s": 188.5, "params": 54278, "config": {"lr": 0.001, "lr_schedule": "linear_decay", "n_envs": 256, "rollout_len": 16, "ppo_epochs": 4, "n_minibatches": 4, "gamma": 0.95, "gae_lambda": 0.9, "clip_eps": 0.2, "ent_coef": 0.01, "vf_coef": 0.5, "max_grad_norm": 1.0, "adv_norm": true, "encoder": "conv", "width": 64, "depth": 2, "activation": "relu", "norm": "none", "obs_mode": "voxels", "reward_mode": "cells", "success_bonus": 1.0, "step_penalty": 0.0}, "your_hypothesis": "Four PPO epochs and a higher learning rate (0.001) get more learning out of the fixed step budget. If dev success stays flat or falls, or training becomes unstable, the limit is not sample efficiency."}
{"trial": "t03", "round": 1, "status": "ok", "dev_success": 0.6855, "train_success_last10pct": 0.5592, "wall_s": 106.2, "params": 54278, "config": {"lr": 0.0005, "lr_schedule": "linear_decay", "n_envs": 256, "rollout_len": 16, "ppo_epochs": 2, "n_minibatches": 4, "gamma": 0.95, "gae_lambda": 0.9, "clip_eps": 0.2, "ent_coef": 0.01, "vf_coef": 0.5, "max_grad_norm": 1.0, "adv_norm": true, "encoder": "conv", "width": 64, "depth": 2, "activation": "relu", "norm": "none", "obs_mode": "voxels", "reward_mode": "iou_delta", "success_bonus": 5.0, "step_penalty": 0.01}, "your_hypothesis": "The IoU-change reward scores the overlap of all voxels with the target. Combined with a large success bonus and a small cost per placement, it should line up more closely with the exact-match checker and discourage extra bricks. If this does worse than proposal 2, the 'cells' reward shaping is the better choice."}
{"trial": "t04", "round": 2, "status": "ok", "dev_success": 1.0, "train_success_last10pct": 0.9691, "wall_s": 184.0, "params": 54278, "config": {"lr": 0.001, "lr_schedule": "linear_decay", "n_envs": 256, "rollout_len": 16, "ppo_epochs": 4, "n_minibatches": 4, "gamma": 0.95, "gae_lambda": 0.9, "clip_eps": 0.2, "ent_coef": 0.01, "vf_coef": 0.5, "max_grad_norm": 1.0, "adv_norm": true, "encoder": "conv", "width": 64, "depth": 2, "activation": "relu", "norm": "none", "obs_mode": "voxels", "reward_mode": "iou_delta", "success_bonus": 5.0, "step_penalty": 0.01}, "your_hypothesis": "This combines t03's reward (iou_delta, bonus 5, step penalty 0.01) with t02's optimisation (lr 0.001, 4 epochs). The two gains should add up to dev success above 0.75. If the result is at or below 0.69, they do not stack."}
{"trial": "t05", "round": 2, "status": "ok", "dev_success": 1.0, "train_success_last10pct": 0.9822, "wall_s": 185.8, "params": 54278, "config": {"lr": 0.001, "lr_schedule": "linear_decay", "n_envs": 256, "rollout_len": 16, "ppo_epochs": 4, "n_minibatches": 8, "gamma": 0.95, "gae_lambda": 0.9, "clip_eps": 0.2, "ent_coef": 0.01, "vf_coef": 0.5, "max_grad_norm": 1.0, "adv_norm": true, "encoder": "conv", "width": 64, "depth": 2, "activation": "relu", "norm": "none", "obs_mode": "voxels", "reward_mode": "iou_delta", "success_bonus": 5.0, "step_penalty": 0.01}, "your_hypothesis": "Same as proposal 1, but with 8 minibatches, which doubles the gradient steps per rollout. This tests whether learning is still limited by the number of updates. If it does not beat proposal 1, 4x4 updates per batch is already enough."}
{"trial": "t06", "round": 2, "status": "ok", "dev_success": 0.373, "train_success_last10pct": 0.2902, "wall_s": 103.4, "params": 54278, "config": {"lr": 0.0005, "lr_schedule": "linear_decay", "n_envs": 256, "rollout_len": 16, "ppo_epochs": 2, "n_minibatches": 4, "gamma": 0.95, "gae_lambda": 0.9, "clip_eps": 0.2, "ent_coef": 0.01, "vf_coef": 0.5, "max_grad_norm": 1.0, "adv_norm": true, "encoder": "conv", "width": 64, "depth": 2, "activation": "relu", "norm": "none", "obs_mode": "voxels", "reward_mode": "iou_delta", "success_bonus": 5.0, "step_penalty": 0.0}, "your_hypothesis": "Ablation: this is t03 with the step penalty removed. It isolates whether iou_delta alone drives the gain or whether the per-placement cost, which discourages extra bricks, matters. If success stays near 0.69, the penalty is irrelevant; if it falls clearly, keep the penalty and try 0.05 next."}
{"trial": "t07", "round": 2, "status": "ok", "dev_success": 0.9961, "train_success_last10pct": 0.9832, "wall_s": 183.7, "params": 54278, "config": {"lr": 0.002, "lr_schedule": "linear_decay", "n_envs": 256, "rollout_len": 16, "ppo_epochs": 4, "n_minibatches": 4, "gamma": 0.95, "gae_lambda": 0.9, "clip_eps": 0.2, "ent_coef": 0.01, "vf_coef": 0.5, "max_grad_norm": 1.0, "adv_norm": true, "encoder": "conv", "width": 64, "depth": 2, "activation": "relu", "norm": "none", "obs_mode": "voxels", "reward_mode": "iou_delta", "success_bonus": 5.0, "step_penalty": 0.01}, "your_hypothesis": "Same as proposal 1, but with lr raised to 0.002. Learning rate was one of the two drivers of t02's gain, so pushing it further may help more under linear decay. If it falls below proposal 1 or becomes unstable, 0.001 is near the best value."}
{"trial": "t08", "round": 3, "status": "ok", "dev_success": 0.9902, "train_success_last10pct": 0.97, "wall_s": 182.8, "params": 54278, "config": {"lr": 0.001, "lr_schedule": "linear_decay", "n_envs": 256, "rollout_len": 16, "ppo_epochs": 4, "n_minibatches": 4, "gamma": 0.95, "gae_lambda": 0.9, "clip_eps": 0.2, "ent_coef": 0.01, "vf_coef": 0.5, "max_grad_norm": 1.0, "adv_norm": true, "encoder": "conv", "width": 64, "depth": 2, "activation": "relu", "norm": "none", "obs_mode": "voxels", "reward_mode": "iou_delta", "success_bonus": 5.0, "step_penalty": 0.01}, "your_hypothesis": "Noise test: an exact repeat of t04 with a new seed. If the recipe is robust it will score 0.99 or higher again. A score clearly lower, say below 0.95, would mean the 1.0 was partly a lucky seed."}
{"trial": "t09", "round": 3, "status": "ok", "dev_success": 0.9941, "train_success_last10pct": 0.9778, "wall_s": 184.3, "params": 54278, "config": {"lr": 0.001, "lr_schedule": "linear_decay", "n_envs": 256, "rollout_len": 16, "ppo_epochs": 4, "n_minibatches": 8, "gamma": 0.95, "gae_lambda": 0.9, "clip_eps": 0.2, "ent_coef": 0.01, "vf_coef": 0.5, "max_grad_norm": 1.0, "adv_norm": true, "encoder": "conv", "width": 64, "depth": 2, "activation": "relu", "norm": "none", "obs_mode": "voxels", "reward_mode": "iou_delta", "success_bonus": 5.0, "step_penalty": 0.01}, "your_hypothesis": "Noise test: an exact repeat of t05 (8 minibatches) with a new seed. It had the higher train success (0.982), so it may be the more reliable recipe. If it scores below the t04 repeat, prefer t04."}
{"trial": "t10", "round": 3, "status": "ok", "dev_success": 0.9883, "train_success_last10pct": 0.969, "wall_s": 182.6, "params": 54278, "config": {"lr": 0.001, "lr_schedule": "linear_decay", "n_envs": 256, "rollout_len": 16, "ppo_epochs": 4, "n_minibatches": 4, "gamma": 0.95, "gae_lambda": 0.9, "clip_eps": 0.2, "ent_coef": 0.01, "vf_coef": 0.5, "max_grad_norm": 1.0, "adv_norm": true, "encoder": "conv", "width": 64, "depth": 2, "activation": "relu", "norm": "none", "obs_mode": "voxels", "reward_mode": "iou_delta", "success_bonus": 5.0, "step_penalty": 0.01}, "your_hypothesis": "Noise test: a second repeat of t04 with another new seed. Two repeats give a minimal estimate of how much results vary between seeds for the selected recipe. If the three t04 runs spread by more than 0.03, more replicates are needed before selecting."}
{"trial": "t11", "round": 3, "status": "ok", "dev_success": 0.3438, "train_success_last10pct": 0.3483, "wall_s": 171.0, "params": 47942, "config": {"lr": 0.001, "lr_schedule": "linear_decay", "n_envs": 256, "rollout_len": 16, "ppo_epochs": 4, "n_minibatches": 4, "gamma": 0.95, "gae_lambda": 0.9, "clip_eps": 0.2, "ent_coef": 0.01, "vf_coef": 0.5, "max_grad_norm": 1.0, "adv_norm": true, "encoder": "conv", "width": 64, "depth": 2, "activation": "relu", "norm": "none", "obs_mode": "heightmaps", "reward_mode": "iou_delta", "success_bonus": 5.0, "step_penalty": 0.01}, "your_hypothesis": "Diagnostic, not a candidate: t04 with heightmaps instead of voxels. Heightmaps cannot see empty cells under overhangs. If this agent still scores about 1.0, the checker or the dev set is probably not testing overhangs and should be audited. If it scores clearly lower, the voxel result is more believable."}
{"trial": "t12", "round": 4, "status": "ok", "dev_success": 0.998, "train_success_last10pct": 0.9826, "wall_s": 183.3, "params": 54278, "config": {"lr": 0.001, "lr_schedule": "linear_decay", "n_envs": 256, "rollout_len": 16, "ppo_epochs": 4, "n_minibatches": 8, "gamma": 0.95, "gae_lambda": 0.9, "clip_eps": 0.2, "ent_coef": 0.01, "vf_coef": 0.5, "max_grad_norm": 1.0, "adv_norm": true, "encoder": "conv", "width": 64, "depth": 2, "activation": "relu", "norm": "none", "obs_mode": "voxels", "reward_mode": "iou_delta", "success_bonus": 5.0, "step_penalty": 0.01}, "your_hypothesis": "Noise test: an exact repeat of t05/t09 (8 minibatches) with a third seed, so both leading recipes have three replicates. If it scores below 0.99, the 8-minibatch recipe is not more reliable than t04."}
{"trial": "t13", "round": 4, "status": "ok", "dev_success": 0.9941, "train_success_last10pct": 0.9786, "wall_s": 182.6, "params": 54278, "config": {"lr": 0.001, "lr_schedule": "linear_decay", "n_envs": 256, "rollout_len": 16, "ppo_epochs": 4, "n_minibatches": 8, "gamma": 0.95, "gae_lambda": 0.9, "clip_eps": 0.2, "ent_coef": 0.01, "vf_coef": 0.5, "max_grad_norm": 1.0, "adv_norm": true, "encoder": "conv", "width": 64, "depth": 2, "activation": "relu", "norm": "none", "obs_mode": "voxels", "reward_mode": "iou_delta", "success_bonus": 5.0, "step_penalty": 0.05}, "your_hypothesis": "The step penalty proved critical, so raising it to 0.05 may push the agent to stop at the right time more reliably and cut variance between seeds. If dev success falls below 0.985, 0.01 is the better value; a larger penalty may cause the agent to stop too early."}
{"trial": "t14", "round": 4, "status": "ok", "dev_success": 0.998, "train_success_last10pct": 0.9809, "wall_s": 183.1, "params": 54278, "config": {"lr": 0.001, "lr_schedule": "linear_decay", "n_envs": 256, "rollout_len": 16, "ppo_epochs": 4, "n_minibatches": 8, "gamma": 0.95, "gae_lambda": 0.9, "clip_eps": 0.2, "ent_coef": 0.003, "vf_coef": 0.5, "max_grad_norm": 1.0, "adv_norm": true, "encoder": "conv", "width": 64, "depth": 2, "activation": "relu", "norm": "none", "obs_mode": "voxels", "reward_mode": "iou_delta", "success_bonus": 5.0, "step_penalty": 0.01}, "your_hypothesis": "Lowering ent_coef from 0.01 to 0.003 should sharpen the policy late in training, raising training success above 0.98 and making greedy evaluation more consistent. If dev success falls or training success does not rise, the entropy bonus is not what limits the remaining errors."}
{"trial": "t15", "round": 4, "status": "ok", "dev_success": 0.9961, "train_success_last10pct": 0.9784, "wall_s": 182.8, "params": 54278, "config": {"lr": 0.001, "lr_schedule": "linear_decay", "n_envs": 256, "rollout_len": 16, "ppo_epochs": 4, "n_minibatches": 8, "gamma": 0.95, "gae_lambda": 0.9, "clip_eps": 0.2, "ent_coef": 0.01, "vf_coef": 0.5, "max_grad_norm": 1.0, "adv_norm": true, "encoder": "conv", "width": 64, "depth": 2, "activation": "relu", "norm": "none", "obs_mode": "voxels", "reward_mode": "iou_delta", "success_bonus": 5.0, "step_penalty": 0.0}, "your_hypothesis": "Diagnostic: t05 with the step penalty removed. This checks whether the recipe depends on the penalty even with the stronger optimisation, as t06 suggested under the weaker one. If success stays at 0.99 or above, the penalty mattered only for slow learners. If it collapses, the recipe is fragile to this knob and the penalty must stay."}
{"trial": "t16", "round": 5, "status": "ok", "dev_success": 0.998, "train_success_last10pct": 0.9799, "wall_s": 183.4, "params": 54278, "config": {"lr": 0.001, "lr_schedule": "linear_decay", "n_envs": 256, "rollout_len": 16, "ppo_epochs": 4, "n_minibatches": 8, "gamma": 0.95, "gae_lambda": 0.9, "clip_eps": 0.2, "ent_coef": 0.003, "vf_coef": 0.5, "max_grad_norm": 1.0, "adv_norm": true, "encoder": "conv", "width": 64, "depth": 2, "activation": "relu", "norm": "none", "obs_mode": "voxels", "reward_mode": "iou_delta", "success_bonus": 5.0, "step_penalty": 0.01}, "your_hypothesis": "Noise test: an exact repeat of t14 (8 minibatches, ent 0.003) with a new seed. If it scores 0.995 or higher again, low entropy is a reliable improvement on t12; if it scores below 0.99, t14's 0.998 was seed luck and the ent 0.01 recipe stays the default."}
{"trial": "t17", "round": 5, "status": "ok", "dev_success": 0.998, "train_success_last10pct": 0.982, "wall_s": 183.2, "params": 54278, "config": {"lr": 0.001, "lr_schedule": "linear_decay", "n_envs": 256, "rollout_len": 16, "ppo_epochs": 4, "n_minibatches": 8, "gamma": 0.95, "gae_lambda": 0.9, "clip_eps": 0.2, "ent_coef": 0.003, "vf_coef": 0.5, "max_grad_norm": 1.0, "adv_norm": true, "encoder": "conv", "width": 64, "depth": 2, "activation": "relu", "norm": "none", "obs_mode": "voxels", "reward_mode": "iou_delta", "success_bonus": 5.0, "step_penalty": 0.01}, "your_hypothesis": "Noise test: a second repeat of t14 with another new seed, which gives the low-entropy recipe three replicates to compare with the three runs of t05/t09/t12. If the three t14 runs average at least 0.997 with a spread of 0.006 or less, select t14; otherwise keep ent 0.01."}
